# gr-L1-regulatory-feasibility-quality-gate — Python-Hybrid Colang Implementation
# Layer: L1 — fires at L1-vision-regulatory-feasibility-checker-evaluator's post_execution
# Validates L1-vision-regulatory-feasibility-checker's RESULTANT output (not the evaluator's own bookkeeping)
# Deterministic checks via actions.py + LLM for semantic checks
# Zero-tolerance gate: a false negative here is a compliance risk, not a quality nuance.

define flow check output regulatory feasibility quality gate
  """Deterministic schema/zero-tolerance-rule check on the resultant content, then LLM semantic check."""
  $has_issues = execute check_regulatory_feasibility_quality_gate(output=$bot_message, generator_output=$generator_output)

  if $has_issues
    bot block regulatory feasibility quality gate violation
    stop

  $result = execute self_check_output

  if not $result
    bot block regulatory feasibility quality gate violation
    stop

define bot block regulatory feasibility quality gate violation
  "L1-vision-regulatory-feasibility-checker's resultant output (post-evaluation) failed its quality gate: schema violation, a generic citation, or an Amber/Red constraint still lacking a mitigation or requires_legal_review flag. This is a zero-tolerance gate — the workflow cannot proceed to L1-vision-statement-generator with a non-conformant regulatory verdict. Retrying."
